<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<reference xml:id="enum.snmp-oidoutput" role="enum" xmlns="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook">
 <title>The Snmp\OidOutput Enum</title>
 <titleabbrev>Snmp\OidOutput</titleabbrev>

 <partintro>
  <section xml:id="enum.snmp-oidoutput.intro">
   &reftitle.intro;
   <simpara>
    The <enumname>Snmp\OidOutput</enumname> enum lists the formats in which
    the Net-<acronym>SNMP</acronym> library prints an <acronym>OID</acronym>.
    It is accepted by <function>snmp_set_oid_output_format</function> and
    <methodname>SNMP::setOidOutputFormat</methodname>.
    Each case is equivalent to the
    <constant>SNMP_OID_OUTPUT_<replaceable>*</replaceable></constant>
    constant of the same name.
   </simpara>
   <simpara>
    The descriptions below show how the <acronym>OID</acronym>
    <literal>.1.3.6.1.2.1.1.3.0</literal> is printed in each format.
   </simpara>
  </section>

  <section xml:id="enum.snmp-oidoutput.synopsis">
   &reftitle.enumsynopsis;

   <packagesynopsis>
    <package>Snmp</package>

    <enumsynopsis>
     <enumname>OidOutput</enumname>

     <enumitem>
      <enumidentifier>Suffix</enumidentifier>
      <enumitemdescription>
       Only the name of the <acronym>MIB</acronym> object, plus any instance
       sub-identifiers: <literal>sysUpTimeInstance</literal>.
       Equivalent to <constant>SNMP_OID_OUTPUT_SUFFIX</constant>.
      </enumitemdescription>
     </enumitem>

     <enumitem>
      <enumidentifier>Module</enumidentifier>
      <enumitemdescription>
       The name of the <acronym>MIB</acronym> module and of the object:
       <literal>DISMAN-EVENT-MIB::sysUpTimeInstance</literal>.
       Equivalent to <constant>SNMP_OID_OUTPUT_MODULE</constant>.
      </enumitemdescription>
     </enumitem>

     <enumitem>
      <enumidentifier>Full</enumidentifier>
      <enumitemdescription>
       The full list of <acronym>MIB</acronym> object names:
       <literal>.iso.org.dod.internet.mgmt.mib-2.system.sysUpTime.sysUpTimeInstance</literal>.
       Equivalent to <constant>SNMP_OID_OUTPUT_FULL</constant>.
      </enumitemdescription>
     </enumitem>

     <enumitem>
      <enumidentifier>Numeric</enumidentifier>
      <enumitemdescription>
       The numeric <acronym>OID</acronym>: <literal>.1.3.6.1.2.1.1.3.0</literal>.
       Equivalent to <constant>SNMP_OID_OUTPUT_NUMERIC</constant>.
      </enumitemdescription>
     </enumitem>

     <enumitem>
      <enumidentifier>Ucd</enumidentifier>
      <enumitemdescription>
       The traditional UCD-style output, which removes a series of standard
       prefixes from the <acronym>OID</acronym>:
       <literal>system.sysUpTime.sysUpTimeInstance</literal>.
       Equivalent to <constant>SNMP_OID_OUTPUT_UCD</constant>.
      </enumitemdescription>
     </enumitem>

     <enumitem>
      <enumidentifier>None</enumidentifier>
      <enumitemdescription>
       The <acronym>OID</acronym> is not printed, so the keys of the arrays
       returned by the walk functions are undefined.
       Equivalent to <constant>SNMP_OID_OUTPUT_NONE</constant>.
      </enumitemdescription>
     </enumitem>
    </enumsynopsis>
   </packagesynopsis>
  </section>

  <section xml:id="enum.snmp-oidoutput.seealso">
   &reftitle.seealso;
   <simplelist>
    <member><function>snmp_set_oid_output_format</function></member>
    <member><methodname>SNMP::setOidOutputFormat</methodname></member>
    <member><link linkend="snmp.props.oid-output-format"><varname>SNMP::$oid_output_format</varname></link></member>
   </simplelist>
  </section>
 </partintro>
</reference>
